WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.045 --> 00:00:17.746
listened very long and hard.

2
00:00:17.766 --> 00:00:19.828
"What do you hear now, Too-Too?"

3
00:00:20.508 --> 00:00:21.509
Dab-Dab asked.

4
00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:26.512
"I don't think it's a man or a woman he said, confused.

5
00:00:28.304 --> 00:00:29.064
Soon Dr.

6
00:00:29.104 --> 00:00:30.785
Dolittle returned with an ax.

7
00:00:30.805 --> 00:00:34.126
"Move back, everyone," he called out.

8
00:00:34.766 --> 00:00:38.327
Dr. Dolittle raised the ax and chopped a hole in the door.

9
00:00:39.127 --> 00:00:41.008
He did it again and again.

10
00:00:41.028 --> 00:00:46.429
"There! Now, let's see who is behind this door," the doctor said.

11
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.330
It was very dark inside.

12
00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.611
Dr. Dolittle found a lamp.

13
00:00:53.471 --> 00:00:54.951
The room was very small.

14
00:00:55.472 --> 00:00:56.812
There were lots of barrels.

15
00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:02.252
"This must be where the pirates keep their rum," said Jip.

16
00:01:04.954 --> 00:01:08.036
In between two barrels sat a little boy crying.

17
00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:10.438
He seemed scared of Dr.

18
00:01:10.478 --> 00:01:14.001
Dolittle. So the doctor spoke gently to him.

19
00:01:14.021 --> 00:01:15.702
"Hello, there."

20
00:01:16.563 --> 00:01:19.385
The boy looked up at the man with the kind voice.

21
00:01:19.405 --> 00:01:21.767
"Are you a pirate?"

22
00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:23.288
the boy asked.

23
00:01:25.871 --> 00:01:28.301
"No. I'm a doctor," Dr.

24
00:01:28.341 --> 00:01:29.261
Dolittle laughed.

25
00:01:29.982 --> 00:01:31.523
The little boy stopped crying.

26
00:01:31.543 --> 00:01:33.745
"Where is my uncle?"

27
00:01:34.426 --> 00:01:34.946
he asked.

28
00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:36.648
"Your uncle?

29
00:01:37.328 --> 00:01:40.090
Well, I don't know," Dr.

30
00:01:40.131 --> 00:01:41.151
Dolittle replied.

31
00:01:42.112 --> 00:01:43.914
The boy started crying again.

32
00:01:49.999 --> 00:01:52.161
Dr. Dolittle took the boy upstairs.

33
00:01:52.181 --> 00:01:54.343
"Do you like biscuits?"

34
00:01:54.903 --> 00:01:55.824
the doctor asked.

35
00:01:56.236 --> 00:01:57.017
"Oh, I do.

36
00:01:57.197 --> 00:01:58.298
Can I have one, please?"

37
00:01:58.738 --> 00:01:59.559
Gub-Gub asked.

38
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.523
After eating a biscuit and drinking some hot tea, the boy told Dr.

39
00:02:04.563 --> 00:02:05.724
Dolittle what happened.

40
00:02:05.744 --> 00:02:08.866
"My uncle and I were fishing.

41
00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:12.609
But the Barbary pirates came and took our boat.

42
00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:15.672
They wanted my uncle to be a pirate!

43
00:02:16.272 --> 00:02:18.754
But my uncle didn't want to be like them."

44
00:02:19.375 --> 00:02:22.117
The boy paused, and the doctor poured him more tea.

45
00:02:22.137 --> 00:02:27.205
"So the pirates got angry," the boy continued.

46
00:02:27.225 --> 00:02:30.748
"They were going to throw my uncle into the ocean.

47
00:02:31.709 --> 00:02:33.570
They put me in the rum room.

48
00:02:34.231 --> 00:02:37.153
And after that, I didn't see my uncle."

49
00:02:37.513 --> 00:02:38.534
He began to cry.

50
00:02:39.435 --> 00:02:41.296
Dr. Dolittle tried to comfort him.

51
00:02:41.316 --> 00:02:42.798
"Don't cry.

52
00:02:43.158 --> 00:02:44.799
Maybe your uncle is fine."

53
00:02:44.819 --> 00:02:47.201
"Ask the dolphins.

54
00:02:47.581 --> 00:02:51.264
Maybe they saw the uncle," Dab-Dab whispered in Dr.

55
00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.125
Dolittle's ear.

56
00:02:52.145 --> 00:02:55.388
"That's a good idea," the doctor replied.

57
00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.961
"What are those sounds you are making?"

58
00:02:58.661 --> 00:02:59.462
the boy asked.

59
00:02:59.482 --> 00:03:04.044
"I'm using duck language," said the doctor, smiling.

60
00:03:05.764 --> 00:03:08.365
The little boy wanted to speak duck language, too.

61
00:03:08.385 --> 00:03:11.087
"What's that strange animal?"

62
00:03:11.867 --> 00:03:13.708
he pointed to the pushmi-pullyu.

63
00:03:13.728 --> 00:03:15.949
"That's a pushmi-pullyu.

64
00:03:16.289 --> 00:03:18.790
He's very shy," the doctor whispered.

65
00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.911
"He's got two heads!"

66
00:03:22.071 --> 00:03:23.132
the boy exclaimed.

67
00:03:25.096 --> 00:03:26.917
"SSSH!" the doctor calmed the boy down.

68
00:03:26.937 --> 00:03:28.758
"Don't talk about his heads.

69
00:03:29.078 --> 00:03:30.059
He's very sensitive."

70
00:03:30.859 --> 00:03:33.321
Dr. Dolittle asked many more questions.

71
00:03:33.821 --> 00:03:35.482
"What does your uncle look like?"

72
00:03:36.903 --> 00:03:38.103
"He has red hair.

73
00:03:38.724 --> 00:03:41.105
My uncle is very strong but kind.

74
00:03:41.725 --> 00:03:43.987
He is the best sailor in the world!"

75
00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:45.608
the boy boasted.

76
00:03:45.628 --> 00:03:47.809
"What is his boat called?"

77
00:03:48.369 --> 00:03:49.590
Dr. Dolittle asked.

78
00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.312
"The Saucy Sally," replied the boy.

79
00:03:54.044 --> 00:03:54.785
"Stay here.

80
00:03:55.265 --> 00:03:57.086
I am going to talk to the dolphins."

81
00:03:57.827 --> 00:03:59.748
With that, the doctor got up.

82
00:04:02.009 --> 00:04:04.051
Dr. Dolittle called the dolphins.

83
00:04:04.071 --> 00:04:05.412
"Hello, Dr.

84
00:04:05.432 --> 00:04:07.193
Dolittle! How was Africa?"

85
00:04:07.773 --> 00:04:08.374
one shouted.

86
00:04:08.394 --> 00:04:09.915
"Oh, lovely!

87
00:04:10.435 --> 00:04:11.796
Can you do something for me?"

88
00:04:12.236 --> 00:04:13.137
the doctor asked.

89
00:04:13.937 --> 00:04:16.539
Of course the dolphins would do anything for Dr.
